# Walkthrough: Smart-search Chrome Extension

I have built the "Smart-search Connector" extension and integrated it with your React frontend. This allows you to save content instantly without leaving the page.

## 📁 Extension Files Created

The extension is located in the `extension/` directory:

- **[manifest.json](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/manifest.json)**: The core manifest defining permissions and background workers.
- **[popup.html](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/popup.html)**: A modern, dark-themed UI with three capture buttons.
- **[popup.js](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/popup.js)**: The logic that captures current tab data and calls the backend.
- **[background.js](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/background.js)**: A service worker that enables right-click "Save Image" and "Save Video" functionality.
- **[content.js](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/content.js)**: A lightweight content script ready for future highlighting/scraping tasks.
- **[icons/](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/extension/icons/)**: Generated placeholder icons for the browser toolbar.

## 🔐 Auth Sync Integration

I modified the following files to ensure the extension stays logged in:

- **[auth.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/Backend/src/controllers/auth.controller.js)**: Now returns the JWT token in the JSON response when you log in or register.
- **[useAuth.jsx](file:///c:/Users/KIIT0001/Desktop/Smart-search/Frontend/src/features/auth/hook/useAuth.jsx)**: Automatically detects the Chrome extension and saves your token to `chrome.storage.local` upon successful login.

## 🚀 How to Install & Test

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Follow these steps to load the extension into your browser:
>
> 1. Open Chrome and go to **`chrome://extensions/`**.
> 2. Enable **Developer mode** in the top-right corner.
> 3. Click **Load unpacked**.
> 4. Select the **`extension/`** folder inside your project directory.
> 5. Log in to your Smart-search web dashboard (this syncs the token).
> 6. Open any website, click the extension icon, or right-click an image to save!

